<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The app has no account, no analytics and no advertising SDK. Nothing it
	     stores (passport stamps, favourites, saved plan, settings) ever leaves
	     the device, so there is no collected data type to declare. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<!-- No tracking, and therefore no tracking domains. Declaring a domain here
	     while the app makes no such request would be a false statement; the one
	     network destination the app can reach (Google Routes, and only after
	     explicit consent) is a functional request, not tracking. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<!-- Required-reason APIs present in the Runner EXECUTABLE.

	     The hand-written Swift (AppDelegate.swift, SceneDelegate.swift) calls
	     none. But Flutter 3.47 links the Swift Package Manager plugins as
	     STATIC libraries, so their native code lands inside the Runner binary
	     and App Store Connect attributes their API use to "Runner". Two of
	     those plugins call a required-reason API and ship an EMPTY
	     NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes in their own manifest (verified in the pub
	     cache, 2026-09-05), so the app manifest must carry the declaration:

	       sensors_plus 7.1.0  FPPStreamHandlerPlus.swift:18
	         ProcessInfo.processInfo.systemUptime — converts CoreMotion sample
	         timestamps to wall-clock time for the compass heading stream.
	         → SystemBootTime, reason 35F9.1 (measure elapsed time between
	           events within the app). Nothing is sent anywhere.

	       package_info_plus 10.2.1  FPPPackageInfoPlusPlugin.m:70
	         -[NSDictionary fileModificationDate] on the app's own bundle
	         path (its install/update date). The plugin is a transitive
	         dependency (geolocator → geolocator_linux) registered on iOS by
	         the Flutter tool; the app never calls it, but the symbol is
	         linked into Runner and the static scan sees it.
	         → FileTimestamp, reason C617.1 (timestamps of files inside the
	           app container). Nothing is sent anywhere.

	     Plugins that DO declare their own use are left to their manifests:
	       shared_preferences_foundation 2.5.6   UserDefaults (1C8F.1)
	       Flutter.framework                     FileTimestamp (0A2A.1,
	                                             C617.1), SystemBootTime
	                                             (35F9.1)
	     No other category (DiskSpace, ActiveKeyboards) is referenced by any
	     linked plugin — grep of every iOS plugin's native sources, 2026-09-05.
	     Guarded by test/unit/ios_privacy_manifest_test.dart. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
